[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 821,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 764,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127325,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 384,
        "headingId": 764,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Gardner fibroma is a benign fibroblastic tumour composed of thick, haphazardly arranged collagen bundles, usually occurring in children and often associated with familial adenomatous polyposis (FAP).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:38:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 822,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 765,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127326,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 384,
        "headingId": 765,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8810/0 Gardner fibroma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:38:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 823,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 766,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127327,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 384,
        "headingId": 766,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>EE6Y &amp; XH7GT0 Other specified fibromatous disorders of skin and soft tissue &amp; Gardner fibroma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:38:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 824,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 767,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127328,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 384,
        "headingId": 767,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> Gardner-associated fibroma.</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> desmoid precursor lesion.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:38:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 825,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 768,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127329,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 384,
        "headingId": 768,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:38:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 826,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 769,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127330,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 384,
        "headingId": 769,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The strongest predilection is for the back and the head and heck region, followed by the extremities and chest wall.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:38:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 827,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 770,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127331,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 384,
        "headingId": 770,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Gardner fibromas are typically solitary but rarely multiple.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:38:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 828,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 771,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127332,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 384,
        "headingId": 771,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most cases occur in children (especially boys); Gardner fibroma is uncommon in adults {17325483}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:38:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 829,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 772,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127333,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 384,
        "headingId": 772,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There is an association with Gardner syndrome {11342777}. They are often associated with desmoid-type fibromatosis {11342777; 17325483}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:38:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 830,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 773,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127334,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 384,
        "headingId": 773,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>FAP-associated tumours have germline mutations in <em>APC</em> {11342777}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:38:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 837,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 780,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127335,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 384,
        "headingId": 780,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are poorly defined tumours with a plaque-like growth pattern, rubbery consistency, and white cut surface. If the lesion contains an apparent fat component, the cut surface may show yellow soft areas. Tumours as large as 120&nbsp;mm can be seen.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:38:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 831,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 774,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127336,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 384,
        "headingId": 774,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours are composed of dense collagen with clefts and cracks and bland spindle cells. Entrapped fat and mast cells can be seen. A helpful diagnostic feature is entrapment of adjacent adipose tissue and neurovascular bundles at the edge of the lesion.</p>\r\n<h6>Immunohistochemistry</h6>\r\n<p>&beta;-catenin is positive {17325483}, and nuclear accumulation of &beta;-catenin is often observed, particularly in cases associated with FAP {17325483; 26840078}. CD34 is almost always positive, whereas SMA is negative {11342777; 17325483}.</p>\r\n<h6>Differential diagnosis</h6>\r\n<p>The differential diagnosis includes nuchal-type fibroma and desmoid-type fibromatosis. Some authors have proposed that a subset of nuchal-type fibromas are in fact Gardner fibromas {11342777}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:38:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 832,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 775,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127337,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 384,
        "headingId": 775,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:38:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 833,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 776,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127338,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 384,
        "headingId": 776,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:38:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 836,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 779,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127339,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 384,
        "headingId": 779,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a plaque-like tumour, commonly arising on the back of the head and neck of young children; dense collagen with clefts and cracks and spindle cells; positive nuclear staining for &beta;-catenin.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> entrapment of adjacent adipose tissue and neurovascular bundles at the edge of the lesion.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:38:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 834,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 777,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127340,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 384,
        "headingId": 777,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:38:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 835,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 778,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127341,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 384,
        "headingId": 778,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Gardner fibroma is a benign tumour with a rate of recurrence as high as 50%. Some patients may develop desmoid-type fibromatosis {11315790; 3760506}.</p>\r\n<p>Given the close association between Gardner fibroma and FAP, a diagnosis of Gardner fibroma should prompt screening of the family for FAP.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:38:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]